NEKO

This is a read-only Linux-inspired shell for exploring the site.

GETTING STARTED
  ls /                  List the virtual root
  tree /post            Browse every post
  cd /post              Change the working directory
  cat path/to/post.md   Read Markdown source
  render path/to/post.md  Render Markdown, formulas, diagrams, and images
  render /slide/example/index.html  Open an HTML slide in a floating window
  theme gruvbox-light  Switch the terminal and page color palette

SHARING
  Add ?blog=/post/name.md to the site URL to render that post on startup.
  Add ?theme=gruvbox-light to select a theme; invalid names use the default.
  Parameters can be combined: ?blog=/post/name.md&theme=gruvbox-light

SHELL FEATURES
  Paths, quoted arguments, wildcards, and pipelines are supported.
  render accepts one .md file or /slide/.../index.html and cannot use a pipeline.
  Use Up/Down for history, Tab for completion, and Ctrl+L to clear.
  Ctrl+C cancels the current line or a running command.

COMMANDS
  [tab] [tab] or `ls /bin` to view all supported command

EXAMPLES
  find /post -type f -name '*.md'
  grep -in terminal /post/**/*.md | head -n 5
  render /post/hello-terminal.md
  render /slide/example/index.html
  printf '%s\n' alpha beta beta | sort | uniq -c

The filesystem is generated from this repository. Add posts, project notes,
and standalone slide directories under content/ to publish them.
